   "text": "I read the drawing region by region and wrote the SMILES from that.\n\n**Left side.** The quinazoline carries:\n- a piperazine on C4;\n- an NH\u2013CH2CH2\u2013C(=O)N(CH3)2 chain on C2;\n- F on C8, a 3-hydroxynaphth-1-yl group on C7, and Cl on C6.\n\n**Linker.** The piperazine nitrogen is acylated by C(=O)\u2013CH=CH\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O)NH\u2013. I took the alkene as trans (E) from its zigzag drawing.\n\n**Right side.** The linker continues into a VHL-type ligand:\n- tert-leucine: NH\u2013CH(tBu)\u2013C(=O)\u2013\n- 4-hydroxyproline\n- an amide to the (1-arylethyl) group, where the aryl is 4-(4-methylthiazol-5-yl)phenyl\n\n**Stereochemistry.** I did not assign the stereocentres directly from the wedges. I took the standard VHL-ligand SMILES as the reference and re-ordered the neighbour lists to match my atom order. The result is the (S)-tert-leucine, (2S,4R)-hydroxyproline and (S)-1-arylethylamine configuration.\n\nSMILES: CN(C)C(=O)CCNc1nc(N2CCN(CC2)C(=O)/C=C/CCOCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N2C[C@H](O)C[C@H]2C(=O)N[C@@H](C)c2ccc(cc2)-c2scnc2C)c2cc(Cl)c(c(F)c2n1)-c1cc(O)cc2ccccc12"
  }
